{
  "note": "Mutants of the limits that a room puts on a map as one set (OnlineLimits: cells, starting ants, pairs of a plant and a waypoint, food objects, power-ups; one MapCounts, one allows / first_over, one table of sentences), for tools/mutate.py (docs/WORKFLOW.md, 'Mutation checks'). Run from the checkout with a configured build folder: python3 tools/mutate.py tests/data/online_terms_mutants.json --keep-going --jobs 1 --timeout 1500. Every mutant must be caught: each breaks one rule of docs/SERVER.md ('Online size limit') or docs/MAP_SUBMISSIONS.md ('The online size limit'): a limit's value, the number that a door reads for it, the order in which the limits are judged, a door that leaves the limits out, a store that does not know a map's counts. The older files of this family (online_limit_mutants.json, online_ants_cap_mutants.json, online_pairs_cap_mutants.json) keep the mutants whose code is still there. Not listed on purpose, as for the ants: the second locks behind a first one that a test does reach (the check in Room::start_lobby and in the lobby's START behind choose_map, load_map and build_room: no door of the manager makes a Room on a map over a limit, so no test can start one; the check of the history's approved-map callback behind the feeder's own load_level). The web side is in tests/data/mapmaker_play_mutants.json (play_food_*, play_powerups_*, play_more_*).",
